Subject: [PATCH] nan_usd: log entry to the action-frame Rx callback

Diagnostic only; not a fix. NAN-USD discovery never completes because
nan_de_rx_sdf() is never called, even though the subscriber's own radio
counts 407 NAN SDFs in 60 s. Review of esp_nan_de_rx_action() shows every
gate in it should pass for those frames, so the open question is whether the
callback is entered at all.

Never printed  -> frames are dropped below the supplicant, in the Wi-Fi
                  libraries or the hardware Rx filter. Note that NAN SDFs
                  carry the NAN Network ID 51:6f:9a:01:00:00 in A1 and A3,
                  which is multicast but not broadcast.
Printed        -> the loss is in the gate chain below, and is fixable here.

MSG_ERROR rather than MSG_DEBUG so the result does not depend on the
reporter's configured log level.

--- a/components/wpa_supplicant/esp_supplicant/src/esp_nan_usd.c
+++ b/components/wpa_supplicant/esp_supplicant/src/esp_nan_usd.c
@@ -141,6 +141,9 @@
 
 int esp_nan_de_rx_action(uint8_t *hdr, uint8_t *payload, size_t len, uint8_t channel)
 {
+    wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "NAN-USD: rx_action entered, len=%u chan=%u",
+               (unsigned)len, (unsigned)channel);
+
     struct ieee80211_hdr *rx_hdr = (struct ieee80211_hdr *)hdr;
     struct nan_de *nan_de = NULL;
     int freq;
